WEBVTT

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:10.290
Yumemi! Come on out, already!

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:12.950
You've patched things up
with the boys in your class.

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:15.370
You can go to school now, right?!

00:00:15.370 --> 00:00:19.950
They weren't picking on me.
You were just jumping to conclusions.

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:23.540
Yu-me-mi!

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:25.790
H-Hatena, no!

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.000
Yumemi!

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:45.450
<i>Tell me, do you remember?</i>

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:49.370
<i>Yes, the wondrous God-given power you have,</i>

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:55.200
<i>like sleight of hand without any tricks?</i>

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:59.000
<i>Tell me, have you already forgotten?</i>

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.160
<i>Those dreamlike, heart-shaped</i>

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:07.540
<i>flower-bouquet-like words of yours?</i>

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:13.830
<i>I'm sure, I'm sure</i>

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:17.450
<i>this key will open your treasure box</i>

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:23.700
<i>and let you remember them tonight</i>

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:26.580
<i>Farewell!</i>

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:27.870
<i>Watch me now,</i>

00:01:27.870 --> 00:01:31.080
<i>I'm gently, quietly going to disappear,</i>

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:33.000
<i>so find me</i>

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:34.200
<i>I'm over here</i>

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:39.330
<i>Our long, long night of secrets is beginning</i>

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:40.620
<i>Come after me</i>

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:45.790
<i>Once you see the twinkle of my tearstains,</i>

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:48.660
<i>catch me with your voice</i>

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:53.410
<i>and the magic words only the two of us know</i>

00:01:59.620 --> 00:02:04.080
When we get home, we have to
convince Yumemi! Work with me, Makoto!

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:06.200
Fighting won't help.

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:16.950
Oh, I have been expecting you.
You are the Hoshisato girl, yes?

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:17.790
Uh...

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:22.040
I am Tominozawa Tomiko. I am a fine art dealer.

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:26.080
I am on good terms with your parents.

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:28.830
I have an exhibition coming up soon.

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:32.000
I wanted to give them this invitation.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:38.870
I would like you to turn over
the golden Artifact that I hear you have.

00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:42.200
Ah, I can hardly wait!

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:43.870
Tominozawa-<i>sama</i>...

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:50.040
Oh, Jeeves, please call me "Tomi-Tomi."

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:55.870
Well, I will see you later.

00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:03.040
The golden Artifact? Does she mean Muff-<i>kun</i>?

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:06.580
Yumemi, are you in there?

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:07.580
Yeah.

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:09.540
Did you go to school today?

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:14.160
No, I didn't. I studied my subjects.

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:17.250
You're going to have dinner with us, right?

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:19.450
I want to eat in my room.

00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:22.790
Yu-me-mi!

00:03:22.790 --> 00:03:25.620
I said no fighting!

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:29.120
I see. Mistress Yumemi again?

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:33.160
Yes. The two of them are being
very stubborn over something.

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:35.790
We have a problem!

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:38.080
What is it, Kokomi?

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:39.330
Just take this.

00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:41.120
Have a look at what's on it.

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:41.370
"Tominozawa Gallery exhibition room"

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:44.160
"Tominozawa Gallery exhibition room"
The Tominozawa Collection
is finally going on display!

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:46.620
So many valuable works of art!

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:47.620
"Tominozawa Gallery exhibition room"

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:53.000
"Tominozawa Gallery exhibition room"
Here, Mr. Cameraman, my precious
works of art. Get a good shot of them.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:53.830
"Tominozawa Gallery exhibition room"
Ah! It's Mama's crest!

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:55.410
Ah! It's Mama's crest!

00:03:55.410 --> 00:03:56.330
Huh?

00:03:56.330 --> 00:04:03.410
We knew that lady was involved
with Artifacts, but Maeve-<i>san</i>'s item, too?

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:06.450
We'll take whatever measures
we can on our end, of course,

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:10.080
but getting that back could
be difficult. What will you do?

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:15.000
Isn't that obvious? The master thief
Hatena will take back the stolen Artifact!

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:16.580
No, you cannot.

00:04:16.580 --> 00:04:19.870
Huh? Why not, Ema-<i>san</i>? If we don't,

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:23.830
then Mama's Artifact might
be used for some evil purposes.

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:27.620
Not until we consult with
the master and the madam first.

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:31.620
Mistress Kana, I cannot allow
you to put yourself in danger.

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:35.200
Can we even be certain that
that one is the genuine article?

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:36.160
Huh?

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:39.750
You're right. She came by
just to deliver those invitations,

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:44.830
and then put herself on TV.
It could be that her true purpose is...

00:04:44.830 --> 00:04:49.910
Yeah! She's trying to lure Hatena out
so she can go after my Muff-<i>kun</i>!

00:04:49.910 --> 00:04:51.370
"My"?

00:04:51.370 --> 00:04:54.540
No, it isn't yours, Kikyouin-<i>san</i>.

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:58.910
We should wait and see
what happens with this development.

00:04:58.910 --> 00:05:03.700
We will deal with it once Mamoru-<i>sama </i>returns.

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:08.910
Make sure not to do
anything rash, Mistress Kana.

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:10.290
All right.

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:12.830
By the way, what is that bear there doing?

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:14.290
Gaugau?!

00:05:15.700 --> 00:05:18.410
She is concerned, all right.

00:05:18.410 --> 00:05:22.120
Hold on, that's the stuffed animal
that the dolly is usually holding, right?

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:25.120
She sent it out to spy on us?

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:32.160
They're after Muff-<i>kun</i>?

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:34.040
Big sister is in trouble.

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:34.870
Gau.

00:05:34.870 --> 00:05:40.660
I know, Gaugau. I've also done
my homework as far as Tominozawa goes.

00:05:40.660 --> 00:05:41.750
Gaugau.

00:05:41.750 --> 00:05:45.250
No? You don't mean that?

00:05:45.250 --> 00:05:47.330
Gau.

00:05:47.330 --> 00:05:51.950
School, huh? What do I do?

00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:57.410
I hate seeing big sister... so sad.

00:05:57.410 --> 00:05:59.330
Hmm?

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:01.580
Are you acting like Makoto-<i>niisama</i>?

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:03.120
Gau.

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:05.580
Makoto-<i>niisama </i>is amazing.

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:10.830
He can do that all on his own,
without using any powers.

00:06:12.790 --> 00:06:16.080
Mm-hmm. Gaugau, if you would?

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:17.620
Gau.

00:06:17.620 --> 00:06:19.580
Huh? A monster scare?

00:06:19.580 --> 00:06:25.700
Word is that a giant bear monster was
sighted over at Kigahara Elementary.

00:06:25.700 --> 00:06:26.580
A bear?

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:30.500
Tokichiro-<i>san</i>, we should find out
the truth of this monster together!

00:06:30.500 --> 00:06:33.200
If it had been a ghost hottie, then maybe.

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:38.500
What's the matter, Makoto?

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:44.750
Oh, sorry, Hatena. I just have something
on my mind. Go on home without me.

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:46.120
Makoto?

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:48.950
--Let's go!
--Mm-hmm!

00:06:48.950 --> 00:06:52.200
Ah, hey, guys!

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:54.540
It's Hoshisato's big brother.

00:06:55.700 --> 00:07:00.580
Hoshisato must really not like me, huh?

00:07:00.580 --> 00:07:03.160
I don't think that's true, actually.

00:07:03.160 --> 00:07:07.080
The reason Hoshisato isn't coming
to school is because of the monster scare.

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:10.000
Rumors are going around
that Hoshisato is behind it.

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:11.540
Yumemi-<i>chan </i>is behind it?

00:07:11.540 --> 00:07:17.700
I joked that the clay figure Hoshisato
made was gross and got smacked.

00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:18.620
By Yumemi-<i>chan</i>?

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:21.500
No! I got smacked by the clay figure!

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:22.330
Huh?

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:25.830
I made a big fuss about it
being a monster figure,

00:07:25.830 --> 00:07:28.250
then Hoshisato stopped coming to school.

00:07:28.250 --> 00:07:31.830
Now there's a rumor that our school is haunted.

00:07:31.830 --> 00:07:34.120
It's not even Hoshisato's fault, either.

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:37.750
Hoshisato... is a really great girl.

00:07:37.750 --> 00:07:43.120
Also, when she smiles, she's kind of...
I mean, <i>really </i>cute.

00:07:44.160 --> 00:07:46.700
--She's cute when she's not smiling.
--She's cute when she's not smiling.

00:07:47.750 --> 00:07:49.370
You idiots! Cut that out!

00:07:49.370 --> 00:07:51.910
Hold it, you guys!

00:07:51.910 --> 00:07:55.950
A clay figure bear came to life, huh?

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:01.950
At last, it's master thief Hatena's first caper.

00:08:01.950 --> 00:08:03.910
What's wrong, Makoto?

00:08:03.910 --> 00:08:07.790
I was just thinking that Ema-<i>san</i>
and Jeeves-<i>san </i>are sure to oppose this.

00:08:07.790 --> 00:08:10.540
You're not suggesting we quit
after coming this far.

00:08:10.540 --> 00:08:16.290
No, I'm not saying that. I, too,
want to do something for Yumemi-<i>chan</i>.

00:08:16.290 --> 00:08:21.000
We're going to take back that clay figure,
and solve Yumemi's problem!

00:08:26.910 --> 00:08:29.660
Ah! That window over there is open, Makoto.

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:33.040
Does that mean...

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:35.580
...someone else has already snuck inside?

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:37.160
Let's go, Makoto.

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:43.870
Ugh, a school is creepy at night, huh?

00:08:43.870 --> 00:08:48.870
Do you think that window might have
been open because of that monster?

00:08:48.870 --> 00:08:52.080
H-Hey, stop that, Makoto.

00:08:52.080 --> 00:08:56.370
I'm not scared, I'm not scared.
We're doing this for Yumemi.

00:08:56.370 --> 00:08:57.410
Found it.

00:08:57.410 --> 00:09:01.450
This bear is like a real-life version of Gaugau.

00:09:01.450 --> 00:09:03.120
It's locked.

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:06.160
Ha, ha, who do you take me for?

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:08.540
Muff-<i>kun</i>, unlock!

00:09:10.950 --> 00:09:11.950
Incredible.

00:09:11.950 --> 00:09:14.950
Nothing is impossible
for the master thief Hatena.

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:29.830
Makoto, um, thanks for everything.

00:09:29.830 --> 00:09:33.000
I'm the master thief
Hatena's partner, after all.

00:09:37.910 --> 00:09:39.660
Is something there?

00:09:46.910 --> 00:09:48.160
Gaugau?

00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:49.750
Wh-What the...?

00:09:51.870 --> 00:09:54.830
Why is there this kind of security
equipment inside a school?

00:09:54.830 --> 00:10:00.620
Ah, I remember! Papa and Mr. Kikyouin
knew we'd be going to school here,

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:03.410
and installed a whole bunch of security systems.

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:04.250
Huh?

00:10:04.250 --> 00:10:09.700
Relax, big sister. I disabled the
security so it won't send any alerts.

00:10:12.410 --> 00:10:13.830
Yumemi?

00:10:13.830 --> 00:10:19.450
Your first master thievery is
being recorded on video for posterity.

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:20.750
Ema-<i>san</i>?

00:10:20.750 --> 00:10:26.120
Now, you two, can I ask you to go
with Gaugau and come back at once?

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:29.910
The time I will spend lecturing you
will eat up your sleeping time.

00:10:29.910 --> 00:10:31.040
--Okay.
--Okay.

00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:36.500
Gaugau was supposed to bring
back the clay bear figure tonight.

00:10:36.500 --> 00:10:37.700
Huh?

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:40.910
I did a preliminary investigation
and got everything ready.

00:10:40.910 --> 00:10:44.830
Then what we thought was
a monster at the school...

00:10:44.830 --> 00:10:47.200
I wish you'd have left this alone.

00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:51.870
Is the clay figurine the reason behind
your school absence, Mistress Yumemi?

00:10:51.870 --> 00:10:53.450
I'm sorry, Yumemi-<i>chan</i>.

00:10:53.450 --> 00:10:58.540
I'm sorry, Yumemi. I was just...

00:10:58.540 --> 00:11:01.830
I know that you were doing it for me.

00:11:01.830 --> 00:11:05.330
Thank you, big sister, Makoto-<i>niisama</i>.

00:11:05.330 --> 00:11:08.830
Huh? So are you going back to school now?

00:11:08.830 --> 00:11:10.540
That has nothing to do with this.

00:11:10.540 --> 00:11:12.410
--Huh?
--Huh?

00:11:12.410 --> 00:11:14.290
See for yourself.

00:11:17.330 --> 00:11:18.160
Huh?

00:11:18.160 --> 00:11:19.790
You mean, that bear...

00:11:19.790 --> 00:11:21.410
...is an Artifact?

00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:23.750
That is correct.

00:11:32.200 --> 00:11:34.620
So how did it go?

00:11:34.620 --> 00:11:39.250
It turns out we still don't know why
Yumemi-<i>chan </i>isn't going to school.

00:11:39.250 --> 00:11:42.120
So it was all for nothing?

00:11:42.120 --> 00:11:44.330
I wonder what we should do.

00:11:44.330 --> 00:11:46.870
You have to do something for her, Makoto-<i>kun</i>.

00:11:46.870 --> 00:11:49.450
You're Hatena's partner, right?

00:11:55.080 --> 00:11:56.830
Hatena...

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:07.330
Take care of it while I'm away, okay?

00:12:08.660 --> 00:12:13.580
Mama... Am I just a failure?

00:12:13.580 --> 00:12:16.370
I hope Yumemi-<i>chan </i>is all right.

00:12:19.330 --> 00:12:20.700
Gaugau?

00:12:24.830 --> 00:12:27.160
I'm only telling this to you.

00:12:28.830 --> 00:12:30.580
Gaugau, you can speak?

00:12:30.580 --> 00:12:35.040
Don't forget my honorific.
I am a lady, after all.

00:12:35.040 --> 00:12:39.000
Oh, sorry. So, Gaugau-<i>chan</i>?

00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:44.580
I only got so I could talk recently.
I haven't even spoken to Yumemi yet.

00:12:44.580 --> 00:12:46.660
Huh? Why not?

00:12:46.660 --> 00:12:50.000
Yumemi has always been
the socially withdrawn type.

00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:51.910
If I'm at her side, and start talking to her,

00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:54.290
she'll find it even harder to make friends.

00:12:54.290 --> 00:12:56.200
That's true.

00:12:56.200 --> 00:12:59.410
So keep the fact that I can talk a secret.

00:12:59.410 --> 00:13:04.540
You're the one Yumemi looks up to the most,
so I need to tell you something.

00:13:04.540 --> 00:13:09.160
Yumemi inherited power as
a practical magician from Maeve-<i>sama</i>.

00:13:09.160 --> 00:13:13.540
But it's not something she ever wanted.

00:13:13.540 --> 00:13:15.410
She knew how Mistress Kana felt

00:13:15.410 --> 00:13:20.120
about wanting to carry on Maeve-<i>sama</i>'s
power more than anyone else.

00:13:20.120 --> 00:13:23.540
She doesn't want to see her big sister look sad.

00:13:23.540 --> 00:13:26.660
She's a good girl,
to care so much for her sister.

00:13:26.660 --> 00:13:32.450
That's why she secretly ordered
me to retrieve the clay figure.

00:13:32.450 --> 00:13:35.410
Did we step all over her plans?

00:13:35.410 --> 00:13:38.830
No. This will all get out sooner or later.

00:13:38.830 --> 00:13:41.830
Yumemi's power is getting stronger and stronger.

00:13:41.830 --> 00:13:44.870
Which is why we need to do something soon.

00:13:44.870 --> 00:13:49.700
Okay, got it. Gaugau-<i>chan</i>, you sure are nice.

00:13:49.700 --> 00:13:53.160
Me being able to talk is
a secret between the two of us.

00:13:53.160 --> 00:13:55.040
Mm-hmm.

00:13:55.040 --> 00:13:56.500
I see,

00:13:56.500 --> 00:13:58.700
so that is what is going on.

00:13:58.700 --> 00:14:02.200
So what should I do?

00:14:02.200 --> 00:14:05.450
I believe there is no
other choice but to use <i>it</i>.

00:14:08.370 --> 00:14:09.950
Yes?

00:14:09.950 --> 00:14:10.950
Kana?

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:13.500
Huh? Mama?

00:14:13.500 --> 00:14:14.830
Mama?!

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:16.330
Mama!

00:14:17.410 --> 00:14:19.620
Kana, I've missed you.

00:14:19.620 --> 00:14:22.540
Mama! Mama! When did you get home?

00:14:22.540 --> 00:14:25.500
There's so much I want to talk to you about!

00:14:25.500 --> 00:14:31.870
Oh, Kana, don't make such a big fuss, now.
You're the older sister...

00:14:34.160 --> 00:14:37.620
Wh-What is that? Jeeves-<i>san</i>! Ema-<i>san</i>!

00:14:37.620 --> 00:14:42.450
I am terribly sorry for that.
The radio waves do not quite seem to be tuned.

00:14:42.450 --> 00:14:44.000
I will go adjust it.

00:14:44.000 --> 00:14:45.250
Radio?!

00:14:45.250 --> 00:14:46.580
Mama...?

00:14:46.580 --> 00:14:51.540
I guess a hastily-made Artifact
doesn't quite cut it, does it?

00:14:51.540 --> 00:14:53.450
I'll have to fix that up later.

00:14:53.450 --> 00:14:55.870
Um, Maeve-<i>san</i>?

00:14:55.870 --> 00:14:59.540
Oh, my, Makoto-<i>kun</i>, you certainly have grown up.

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:02.120
Did that thing I gave you come in handy?

00:15:02.120 --> 00:15:03.660
Oh, yes.

00:15:04.790 --> 00:15:07.830
I'm glad you held on to it so carefully.

00:15:07.830 --> 00:15:11.000
I know you'll be able to use it quite well.

00:15:12.540 --> 00:15:15.950
Mama, what's going on?

00:15:15.950 --> 00:15:21.290
This is an Artifact-produced...
well, duplicate of myself, sort of.

00:15:21.290 --> 00:15:24.790
Then, you aren't actually here, are you?

00:15:24.790 --> 00:15:29.290
No. Things have gotten quite
unpleasant with your grandmother.

00:15:29.290 --> 00:15:33.450
It looks like it will be a while
longer before I can actually return.

00:15:33.450 --> 00:15:35.250
Oh, okay.

00:15:35.250 --> 00:15:38.200
Ah, you know what, Mama? Yumemi is...

00:15:38.200 --> 00:15:45.120
I heard all about it from Ema.
It's all right. I'll speak to Yumemi.

00:15:45.120 --> 00:15:51.580
You've been doing your best while
I'm away, I see. Thank you, Kana.

00:15:51.580 --> 00:15:53.000
Mama...

00:15:59.200 --> 00:16:01.910
Yumemi, it's me.

00:16:03.330 --> 00:16:06.620
Mother? Mother!

00:16:06.620 --> 00:16:10.290
Mother... are you...?

00:16:10.290 --> 00:16:14.120
I should have known
you'd figure it out immediately.

00:16:14.120 --> 00:16:17.540
I'm sorry I couldn't come see you in person.

00:16:17.540 --> 00:16:23.200
Mm-mm, that's okay. Anything is fine,
as long as we can be together.

00:16:23.200 --> 00:16:27.160
Okay. Yumemi, you really
are trying your hardest, huh?

00:16:27.160 --> 00:16:31.040
Mm-hmm. But it's not going so well.

00:16:31.040 --> 00:16:33.830
I've tried to keep it
from working, but it's no use.

00:16:33.830 --> 00:16:38.540
You can't help it. No one has taught you how.

00:16:38.540 --> 00:16:44.250
I'm sorry. If I was there at your side,
I could show you how to control it.

00:16:44.250 --> 00:16:46.290
I can do it, too?

00:16:46.290 --> 00:16:47.910
Of course.

00:16:47.910 --> 00:16:52.330
I figured this day would come eventually,

00:16:52.330 --> 00:16:54.910
and that's why I gave you Gaugau as a present.

00:16:54.910 --> 00:16:56.700
You did?

00:16:56.700 --> 00:17:00.580
Your power is influenced by strong emotions.

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:03.450
Artifacts that are made when you are angry

00:17:03.450 --> 00:17:06.700
can turn out to be aggressive, dangerous things.

00:17:06.700 --> 00:17:11.620
That clay figurine having a mind
of its own is a result of that.

00:17:11.620 --> 00:17:14.040
Is it because I'm not yet emotionally mature?

00:17:14.040 --> 00:17:16.790
It's why when you try to enchant
something with your power,

00:17:16.790 --> 00:17:19.910
it's important to be calm and level-headed.

00:17:19.910 --> 00:17:25.790
Our ancestors would shower with cold water,
and meditate for several hours.

00:17:25.790 --> 00:17:29.540
Ugh, I hate being cold.

00:17:29.540 --> 00:17:35.620
It's hard on me, too. There's one
other thing I want you to remember.

00:17:35.620 --> 00:17:40.620
You cannot become too emotional,
but that that isn't a hard and fast rule.

00:17:40.620 --> 00:17:45.410
There are times when strong feelings
give a positive outcome to an Artifact.

00:17:45.410 --> 00:17:48.500
Yumemi, do you like Gaugau?

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:50.450
I do. We're always together.

00:17:50.450 --> 00:17:51.500
Gau.

00:17:51.500 --> 00:17:57.790
Glad to hear it. I created Gaugau
while I was thinking of you, Yumemi.

00:17:57.790 --> 00:18:03.540
"Let Yumemi be happy," and
"Let Yumemi be able to smile."

00:18:03.540 --> 00:18:05.330
Gaugau.

00:18:05.330 --> 00:18:08.160
Mm-hmm. I love you, Gaugau.

00:18:08.160 --> 00:18:13.290
Keep practicing a little at a time.
You may not do well at first,

00:18:13.290 --> 00:18:15.330
but I know you can do it.

00:18:15.330 --> 00:18:18.700
You have Gaugau there with you,
as well as Makoto.

00:18:18.700 --> 00:18:22.660
Ema and Jeeves are in your corner, as well.

00:18:22.660 --> 00:18:28.080
Also, turn even more to
the sister you love so much.

00:18:28.080 --> 00:18:30.500
Mm-hmm, I'll try.

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:33.700
Thanks for waiting.

00:18:33.700 --> 00:18:36.370
Mama! Yumemi!

00:18:36.370 --> 00:18:42.120
I know you were worried,
but Yumemi is okay now. Right, Yumemi?

00:18:43.580 --> 00:18:45.120
Thank goodness.

00:18:45.120 --> 00:18:46.370
Mama!

00:18:49.080 --> 00:18:53.620
Listen up, you two. No matter what you do,

00:18:53.620 --> 00:18:58.330
do not tell anyone that Yumemi can
create Artifacts. If anyone found out...

00:18:58.330 --> 00:19:00.700
Yumemi would be targeted?

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:05.290
That's right. I fear your grandmother
coming after her more than anything.

00:19:05.290 --> 00:19:09.540
Morrigan L'lhuta-<i>sama</i>,
the elder who presides over the family.

00:19:09.540 --> 00:19:13.330
Please consider her to be
a hard-nosed, stubborn old <i>bat</i>.

00:19:13.330 --> 00:19:15.370
J-Jeeves-<i>san</i>...

00:19:15.370 --> 00:19:17.700
That was my description for her.

00:19:17.700 --> 00:19:19.950
Heh, heh, I borrowed it.

00:19:19.950 --> 00:19:23.910
If she finds out, I'm sure she will
try to take you back to her village.

00:19:23.910 --> 00:19:26.290
So be careful, Yumemi.

00:19:26.290 --> 00:19:30.120
Kana, please, keep Yumemi safe.

00:19:30.120 --> 00:19:33.950
Mm-hmm, leave it to me!
She's my dear sister, after all!

00:19:33.950 --> 00:19:39.700
Thank you, Kana. You are always
a daughter I can take pride in.

00:19:41.540 --> 00:19:43.410
Mother...

00:19:44.750 --> 00:19:47.910
Makoto-<i>kun</i>, please watch
over Kana and Yumemi, too.

00:19:47.910 --> 00:19:49.700
R-Right.

00:20:00.950 --> 00:20:03.040
I'm home, my honeys!

00:20:03.040 --> 00:20:06.660
Hoshisato Mamoru has just made his come-back!

00:20:08.410 --> 00:20:11.700
Well, well, what's the matter, my daughters?

00:20:11.700 --> 00:20:14.160
Your beloved papa has returned.

00:20:14.160 --> 00:20:17.120
Here, feel free to leap into your papa's arms.

00:20:17.120 --> 00:20:18.950
--Sorry, Papa, another time.
--Huh?

00:20:18.950 --> 00:20:22.500
--Father, read the room.
--Huh? Huh?

00:20:22.500 --> 00:20:26.160
No! A rebellious phase?

00:20:26.160 --> 00:20:30.500
How come, Yumemi? You told Mama
you were going to school, right?

00:20:30.500 --> 00:20:34.000
No I didn't. I'm too busy
practicing controlling my power.

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:36.000
Well, when are you going to start going?

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:38.950
Once I can control my creation of Artifacts.

00:20:38.950 --> 00:20:42.790
Yu-me-mi!

00:20:42.790 --> 00:20:45.370
Hatena, no!

00:20:45.370 --> 00:20:49.330
Oh, I have an idea. Yumemi, you should
be the one to have that crest.

00:20:49.330 --> 00:20:52.700
If you have that, you'll be able
to control your Artifacts, right?

00:20:52.700 --> 00:20:58.450
Big sister, you dummy.
You didn't listen to what Mother said.

00:20:58.450 --> 00:21:01.370
That belongs to you.

00:21:01.370 --> 00:21:06.750
But I don't have the power to create Artifacts!

00:21:06.750 --> 00:21:11.330
Yumemi, you're the one...
who takes more after Mother.

00:21:11.330 --> 00:21:19.450
I'm not at all like Mother.
But even so, I'm still your big sister!

00:21:19.450 --> 00:21:24.040
I will keep you safe,
and I will collect Mother's Artifacts,

00:21:24.040 --> 00:21:26.450
and lock them up, too!

00:21:26.450 --> 00:21:28.450
Big sister, you dummy.

00:21:29.750 --> 00:21:32.330
You really are dumb.

00:21:32.500 --> 00:21:38.290
<i>My path now begins</i>

00:21:38.290 --> 00:21:46.660
<i>I've unleashed the hidden light of one future</i>

00:21:50.370 --> 00:21:53.040
<i>I've been on the hunt</i>

00:21:53.040 --> 00:21:57.080
<i>to find my furthest dreams</i>

00:21:57.080 --> 00:22:00.250
<i>I want to shine even brighter</i>

00:22:00.250 --> 00:22:05.370
<i>The "someday" that my former self prayed for</i>

00:22:05.370 --> 00:22:10.540
<i>is still far away, but I'll catch up</i>

00:22:10.540 --> 00:22:15.540
<i>"Miracle" is such an embarrassingly vague word</i>

00:22:15.540 --> 00:22:20.700
<i>My timeframe has neither forever nor a moment</i>

00:22:20.700 --> 00:22:27.950
<i>I move forward one step at a time to my voice</i>

00:22:27.950 --> 00:22:31.750
<i>No matter what awaits me</i>

00:22:31.750 --> 00:22:33.080
<i>beyond this pain</i>

00:22:33.080 --> 00:22:35.330
<i>I'll once again, yes once again</i>

00:22:35.330 --> 00:22:38.080
<i>leap up and shine</i>

00:22:38.080 --> 00:22:41.910
<i>Yeah, I'll put into words</i>

00:22:41.910 --> 00:22:43.500
<i>the view laid out before me</i>

00:22:43.500 --> 00:22:46.750
<i>and let it ring out dozens,</i>

00:22:46.750 --> 00:22:50.410
<i>even hundreds of times</i>

00:22:50.410 --> 00:22:54.700
<i>What color do you suppose love is?</i>

00:22:54.700 --> 00:23:00.370
<i>I've unleashed my hidden light</i>

00:23:02.620 --> 00:23:06.330
Yumemi is just concerned about me.

00:23:06.330 --> 00:23:09.250
If only Mama were here...

00:23:09.250 --> 00:23:13.580
Do you want me to tell you a way
to bring Maeve-<i>neesan </i>back home?

00:23:13.580 --> 00:23:15.200
Auntie Mariah!

00:23:15.200 --> 00:23:18.330
Would you mind not calling me "Auntie"?

00:23:18.330 --> 00:23:21.250
A way to bring Mother home?

00:23:21.250 --> 00:23:28.950
Yes, using your own power.
If you're interested, come here tomorrow.

00:23:32.250 --> 00:23:39.040
"What have you recently
shopped for on the Internet?"

00:23:40.000 --> 00:23:52.080
"Maeve"

00:23:52.080 --> 00:24:02.000
"See you next time"
